==Premise==
The [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 1|first season]] follows [[S.H.I.E.L.D. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|S.H.I.E.L.D.]] agent [[Phil Coulson]] as he puts together a small team of agents to handle strange new cases.<ref name="Apr2013ABCAllAccess" /> They investigate [[Project Centipede]] and its leader, "[[John Garrett (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|The Clairvoyant]]", eventually uncovering that the organization is backed by the terrorist group [[Hydra (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hydra]], which has infiltrated S.H.I.E.L.D. In the [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 2|second season]], following the destruction of S.H.I.E.L.D. in ''[[Captain America: The Winter Soldier]]'' (2014), Coulson becomes director of the organization and is tasked with rebuilding it while dealing with Hydra, a faction of anti-superhuman S.H.I.E.L.D. agents, and a newly-revealed superhuman race called the [[Inhumans (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Inhumans]].<ref name="S2Synopsis" /><ref name="Daisy" />

In the [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 3|third season]], Coulson begins a secret mission to assemble the [[Secret Warriors (Team White)|Secret Warriors]], a team of Inhumans,<ref name="SHIELDS3Returners" /><ref name="S3SecretWarriors" /> as Hydra restores its ancient Inhuman leader [[Hive (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Hive]] to power.<ref name="Hive" /> After the defeat of Hive and Hydra, S.H.I.E.L.D. is made a legitimate organization once again with the signing of the [[Sokovia Accords]]. In the [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 4|fourth season]], Coulson returns to being a field agent so S.H.I.E.L.D. can have a public leader, and is tasked with tracking down more enhanced people, including [[Robbie Reyes (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Robbie Reyes / Ghost Rider]]. In addition, Agent [[Leo Fitz]] and [[Holden Radcliffe (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Holden Radcliffe]] complete their work on the [[Life Model Decoy (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Life Model Decoy]] and Framework virtual reality projects.<ref name="S4Premise" />

The [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 5|fifth season]] sees Coulson and members of his team abducted to the space station Lighthouse in the year 2091, where they must try to save the remnants of humanity while figuring out how to get home.<ref name="S5Premise" /> After returning to the present, where they are labeled fugitives, Coulson and his team work to prevent the future that they saw.<ref name="2018OlympicsBreak" /> They succeed in defeating a [[Gravitonium]]-powered [[Glenn Talbot (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Glenn Talbot]], but Coulson dies due to his interactions with Ghost Rider in the previous season.<ref name="CoulsonFirstTeaser" />

In the [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 6|sixth season]], the S.H.I.E.L.D. agents are divided into two groups: one heads to space to find Fitz, who is lost following the last season's time-traveling,<ref name="WonderCon2019WhedonTancharoen" /><ref name="WonderCon2019HenstridgeBell" /> while the other remains on Earth to face a team of mercenaries led by [[Sarge (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sarge]], a man that looks just like Coulson.<ref name="WonderCon2019WhedonTancharoen" /><ref name="WonderCon2019HenstridgeBell" /><ref name="Sarge" /> The [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. season 7|seventh]] and final season finds the team, including a Life Model Decoy of Coulson,<ref name="CoulsonLMD" /> jumping throughout time to prevent the [[Chronicoms (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Chronicoms]] from establishing Earth as their new home, Chronyca-3, and eradicating S.H.I.E.L.D. from history.<ref name="S7Premise" /><ref name="CBRS7Premise" />

